  "notes": "Read from the user's own AutoCAD detail, not from a manufacturer table. The product codes and the section sizes are what that detail calls up. The spacings are what that detail was set out at on that job - they are NOT known to be the manufacturer's maxima, and entering them here as maxima is an assumption the user has to check against the current Rondo and Flexistrut literature before this pack is used on anything. Span figures and load cases are blank because the detail does not carry them. This is a four-tier suspension: the slotted angle is fixed across the joists, an M10 rod hangs the strut from it, an M6 rod hangs the top cross rails from the strut, and the furring channel clips up under the rails.",
